:"Jeremiah","H854":"with","H3068":"LORD","H559":"to say","H6965":"(Leb)-kamai","H3381":"to go down","H1004":"place","H3335":"formed","H8033":"there","H8085":"hear","H853":"[Obj.]","H2009":"behold","H1931":"he/she/it","H6213":"do","H4399":"work","H5921":"upon","H70":"wheel","H7843":"to ruin","H3627":"article/utensil","H2563":"clay","H3027":"hand","H7725":"return","H312":"another","H3474":"to smooth","H5869":"eye","H2088":"this","H3808":"not","H3201":"be able","H3478":"Israel","H5002":"utterance","H3651":"right","H859":"you(m.s.)","H7281":"moment","H1696":"speak","H1471":"nation","H4467":"kingdom","H5428":"to uproot","H5422":"to tear","H6":"to perish","H7451":"harmful","H5162":"comfort","H2803":"design","H1129":"to build","H5193":"to plant","H1115":"lest","H6963":"voice","H2896":"pleasant","H3190":"be good","H6258":"now","H4994":"please","H376":"man","H3063":"Judah","H3427":"to dwell","H3389":"Jerusalem","H3541":"thus","H595":"I","H4284":"plot","H1870":"conduct","H4611":"deed","H2976":"to despair","H3588":"for","H310":"after","H3212":"to walk","H8307":"stubbornness","H3820":"heart","H7592":"to ask","H4310":"who?","H428":"these","H8186":"horror","H3966":"much","H1330":"virgin","H5800":"forsake","H6697":"Rocks (of Goats)","H7704":"Sirion","H7950":"snow","H3844":"Lebanon","H518":"if","H4325":"water","H2114":"be a stranger","H7119":"cool","H5140":"to flow","H7911":"to forget","H5971":"people","H7723":"false","H6999":"burn","H3782":"to stumble","H7635":"path","H5769":"enduring","H5410":"path","H5549":"to build","H7760":"make","H776":"country/planet","H8047":"destroyed","H8292":"piping","H8322":"hissing","H3605":"all","H5674":"to pass","H8074":"destroyed","H5110":"to wander","H7218":"head","H7307":"spirit","H6921":"east","H6327":"to scatter","H6440":"before","H341":"enemy","H6203":"neck","H7200":"see","H3117":"day","H343":"calamity","H8451":"instruction","H3548":"priest","H6098":"counsel","H2450":"wise","H5030":"prophet","H5221":"to smite","H3956":"tongue","H408":"not","H7181":"to listen","H3401":"opponent","H7999":"to complete","H8478":"under","H3738":"to dig","H7745":"pit","H5315":"soul","H2142":"to remember","H5975":"stand","H2534":"rage","H5414":"give","H1121":"child","H7458":"famine","H5064":"to pour","H2719":"sword","H802":"woman","H7909":"childless","H490":"widow","H2026":"to kill","H4194":"death","H970":"youth","H4421":"battle","H2201":"outcry","H935":"come","H1416":"band","H6597":"suddenly","H7882":"pit","H3920":"to capture","H6341":"snare","H2934":"to hide","H7272":"foot","H3045":"to know","H3722":"to atone","H5771":"crime","H2403":"sin","H4229":"to wipe","H6256":"time","H639":"anger"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["challoner",20,null,"challoner","Remember, etc.... This is spoken in the person of Christ, persecuted by the Jews, and prophetically denouncing the evils that should fall upon them in punishment of their crimes."],["haydock",2,null,"haydock","Potter's. Thus God would shew his dominion over all. Rom. ix. 21."],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","Wheel. Hebrew \"stones.\" Septuagint \"seats;\" or \"wheel.\" Chaldean Ex. i. 16. See Eccle. xxxviii. 32. (Calmet)"],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","Broken. So Providence ordered it. (St. Jerome) — How should this idea humble man! (Calmet) — A potter may mould afresh the clay as long as it is soft, but God can change the hardest heart. (Worthington)"],["haydock",8,null,"jerome","Shall repent, having free-will, though prevented by grace. (St. Jerome)"],["haydock",12,null,"haydock","Hopes. C. ii. 25. Septuagint \"we are valiant men.\" (Haydock)"],["haydock",13,null,"haydock","Virgin. The disorders of Israel are thus enhanced. (Calmet)"],["haydock",14,null,"haydock","Snow. It continues on Libanus seven or eight months, (La Roque quoted. Univ. Hist. ii. p. 363) or all the year; (Tacit. Hist. v. 6.) and hence the mountain is justly denominated \"white,\" as the Alps and Albion are from albon. Bochart. Parkhurst, p. 155. (Haydock) — Away. Yet my people abandon me, to serve idols! Hebrew may have many other senses to the same purpose. Septuagint \"Shall the mountain springs fail, or snow from Libanus? Shall a stream forcibly driven by the wind, turn aside?\" (Haydock) — The laws of nature are observed by inanimate things, and shall my people be so foolish as to follow mere vanity."],["haydock",15,null,"haydock","Ancient; followed by the patriarchs. C. vi. 16."],["haydock",16,null,"haydock","Head, through contempt (Calmet) and pity. Lam. ii. 15."],["haydock",17,null,"jerome","Burning. Hebrew kadim, \"eastern,\" (Haydock) coming from Desert Arabia. Ex. x. 13. (Calmet) — Back. Thus the Lord now treats the synagogue. (St. Jerome)"],["haydock",18,null,"haydock","Prophet. Jeremias will not cease to upbraid us with our transgressions; or we have guides as good as him, and we shall not be left destitute, as he would intimate. — Tongue, detraction; or make him suffer for what he says. In all the transactions of this prophet, Christ was foreshewn; (Calmet) and here, particularly, the Jews demand the crucifixion. (St. Jerome; Worthington)"],["haydock",20,null,"haydock","Remember, &c. This is spoken in the person of Christ, persecuted by the Jews, and prophetically denouncing the evils that should fall upon them in punishment for their crimes. (Challoner) — Jeremias had prayed earnestly for the people. C. xiv. 17. (Haydock)"],["haydock",21,null,"haydock","Therefore. He foretells of the event, and approves of the chastisement of the impenitent, (Calmet) whose \"impurity might be a bad precedent for others. S. Jer. See C. xvii. 18."],["haydock",22,null,"haydock","For. Protestants \"when.\" (Haydock) — Robber. So Nabuchodonosor and all professional conquerors are styled. (Calmet)"],["haydock",23,null,"haydock","Destroy. Hebrew \"with them.\" use them as vessels of ignominy: abutere. (Haydock)"]],"au":{"challoner":["Richard Challoner",0,0,1781,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/03566a.htm"],"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"],"jerome":["Jerome",1,1,420,"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/#jerome"]},"fa":[[3,6,0,"Instructions to Catechumens","First Instruction",0,407,"… But when he wishes to hold out good hopes to them, he brings the prophet to a pottery, and does not show him an earthen vessel, but shows him a vessel of clay, which was in the hands of the potter, falling to the ground: and brings him to it saying, \"If this potter has taken up and remodelled his vessel which has fallen, shall I not much rather be able to restore you when you have fallen? …"],[7,10,1,"Conferences of John Cassian - Part II","17. The Second Conference of Abbot Joseph",1,435,"… If that nation repent of the evil, which I have spoken against it, I also will repent of the evil which I thought to do to them. And I will suddenly speak of a nation and a kingdom, to build up and to plant it. If it shall do evil in My sight, that it obey not My voice: I will repent of the good that I thought to do to it. To Ezekiel also: \"Leave out nota word, if so be they will hearken and be converted every one from his evil way: that I may repent Me of the evil that I thought to do to them for the wickedness of their doings. …"]],"fau":[["chrysostom","John Chrysostom",1,"father",null,1,407],["cassian","John Cassian",0,"father",null,0,435]],"ftr":[["Nicene and Post-Nicene Fathers, series 1, vol. 9 (1889)","https://ccel.org/ccel/schaff/npnf109"],["Nicene and Post-Nicene Fathers, series 2, vol. 11 (1894)","https://ccel.org/ccel/schaff/npnf211"]]}